d requesting an apology for all women. She also asked for a response to emails and\nphone calls.\n\nMayor Butts recessed the City Council at the hour of 3:10 p.m. for Closed Session Item\nNo. CS-1.\n\n  *****************\n\nMayor Butts reconvened the City Council at the hour of 3:15 p.m. for Closed Session\nItem No. CS-1.\n\nCLOSED SESSION – PENDING LITIGATION WITH LEGAL COUNSEL AND\nCLAIMANT T.DOE. Closed Session – Confidential – Attorney/Client Privileged; City\nCouncil Conference with Legal Counsel – Anticipated Litigation Pursuant to Government\nCode Section 54956.9(d)(2); One Potential Case: Claim of T. Doe.\n\nIt was moved by Council Member Dotson, and seconded by Council Member Faulk that\nthe City Council does hereby reject the claim of T. Doe. The motion was carried by the\nfollowing roll call vote:\nAyes:  Council Members Dotson, Padilla, and Faulk;\nNoes:  None;\nAbstain: Mayor Butts; and\nAbsent: Council Member Morales.\n\nThere being no further business to be presented, Mayor Butts declared the meeting\nadjourned at the hour of 3:17 p.m.\n\nApproved this 17th day of August, 2021\n\n  _________________________\n  Aisha L. Thompson, City Clerk\n\n________________________\nJames Butts, Jr., Mayor","tries":1}